# Optional connection config for `test.sh` — copy to `.env` to point the test at ANY RabbitMQ with one value.
#   cp .env.example .env        # then uncomment ONE option below
# `.env` is gitignored. test.sh uses this only when you DON'T pass a TARGET arg or RABBITMQ_URL.
# (Priority: a URL arg / RABBITMQ_URL > THIS .env > a per-variant .env > parts/defaults 127.0.0.1:15672.)
# The test talks to the Management HTTP API (port 15672), so it needs only curl.

# Option A — a single management URL (with credentials):
# RABBITMQ_URL=http://dokandar:yourpassword@127.0.0.1:15672

# Option B — individual parts:
# RABBITMQ_HOST=127.0.0.1
# RABBITMQ_MGMT_PORT=15672
# RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER=dokandar
# RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS=yourpassword
